<p>These endpoints work fine locally because I&#x27;ve set the <code>DATABASE_URL</code> environment variable in my <code>local.settings.json</code> file,
however my deployed Function doesn&#x27;t have this setting.</p>
<p>Luckily, Azure Functions makes it easy to set environment variables for your function app.
Just run the following command to set the <code>DATABASE_URL</code> environment variable to the connection string for my Neon database:</p>
<p>Define an environment variable in the Azure Function App settings to store the database connection string, using this command:</p>
